---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About · jongio/skills" description="About jongio/skills — a cross-agent collection of skills for AI coding agents.">
  <header style="text-align:center;">
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.75rem,5vw,2.5rem);margin:0 0 .75rem;">About</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/jongio/skills">jongio/skills</a> is Jon Gallant's
      collection of reusable skills for AI coding agents, plus a live session
      footer for Copilot CLI. Install a skill for a specific task, or the full collection.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      A skill gives your agent a repeatable way to handle a task, such as checking
      dependencies, setting up a repository, or explaining an error. In Copilot,
      invoke an installed skill with <code>/&lt;skill-name&gt;</code> and describe what you need.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Works across agents</h2>
    <p>
      The skills use the <a href="https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills">SKILL.md</a>
      format and <a href="https://agent-plugins.org/plugin-authors/manifest">Agent Plugins 1.0</a>,
      so they work with <strong>GitHub Copilot</strong> (App, CLI, VS Code, and coding agent),
      <strong>Claude Code</strong>, <strong>Codex</strong>, <strong>Cursor</strong>,
      <strong>Gemini CLI</strong>, and any host that supports them. Add the repo as a
      marketplace, install individual skills, or install the whole collection as one plugin.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Installation steps differ by app. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/jongio/skills#app-and-editor-support">support matrix</a>
      for your editor or agent, including web, mobile, and IDE limitations.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Copilot CLI statuslines</h2>
    <p>
      Four footer components show your session's <strong>Branch and Worktree</strong>,
      <strong>Pull Requests</strong>, <strong>Issues</strong>, and <strong>Subagents</strong>.
      See where the agent is working, whether commits are missing, which PR checks
      need attention, and how background work is progressing. Related PRs and
      issues stay beside their checkout.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      These are Copilot CLI–only extensions (they automatically no-op in the GitHub
      Copilot app). Use <code>/session-statusline setup</code> (or <code>/statusline-setup</code>)
      to choose components, <code>/session-statusline name &lt;label&gt;</code> to label the
      session, <code>/session-statusline refresh | clear</code> to refresh or clear tracked
      items, <code>/session-worktree</code> to inspect checkouts, and <code>/session-attention</code>
      for Windows Terminal attention alerts.
      See the <a href="/skills/statuslines/">statuslines guide</a> for the grouped
      footer illustration and the meaning of <code>*</code>, <code>+</code>,
      <code>%</code>, <code>↑</code>, <code>↓</code>, and <code>?</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p><strong>1 · Cross-platform one-liner (Copilot, Claude, Codex &amp; Gemini CLIs):</strong></p>
    <p class="muted">Runs the native plugin install in every detected CLI first and then removes only provenance-verified conflicting raw copies from <code>~/.copilot/skills</code>, <code>~/.claude/skills</code>, and <code>~/.agents/skills</code> (unrelated or hand-authored skills are preserved, and shared <code>~/.agents/skills</code> and <code>~/.codex/skills</code> entries stay intact when another consumer such as Codex IDE or Cline is present unless <code>-CleanShared</code> / <code>--clean-shared</code> or <code>-CleanOnly</code> / <code>--clean-only</code> is passed in a local checkout):</p>
    <pre><code>irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jongio/skills/main/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>
    <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jongio/skills/main/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
    <p><strong>2 · Per-agent native plugin install (global &amp; namespaced):</strong></p>
    <p class="muted">In Copilot CLI or Claude Code:</p>
    <pre><code>/plugin marketplace add jongio/skills</code></pre>
    <pre><code>/plugin install jongio-skills@jongio-skills</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">Or install just the Copilot CLI statuslines (without skills):</p>
    <pre><code>/plugin install statuslines@jongio-skills</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">In Codex CLI:</p>
    <pre><code>codex plugin marketplace add jongio/skills &amp;&amp; codex plugin add jongio-skills</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">In Gemini CLI:</p>
    <pre><code>gemini extensions install https://github.com/jongio/skills --consent</code></pre>
    <p><strong>3 · Project-scoped install via Skills CLI (<code>npx skills</code>):</strong></p>
    <p class="muted">Install into the current repository without touching <code>~/.agents/skills</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>npx skills add jongio/skills --skill create-canvas-app</code></pre>
    <pre><code>npx skills add jongio/skills --all</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">
      Browse all skills in <a href="/skills/catalog/">the catalog</a> or view the <a href="/skills/statuslines/">Copilot CLI statuslines guide</a>.
      In Copilot CLI, start a new session after installing extensions (and enable experimental SDK extensions once with <code>/settings experimental on</code> followed by <code>/restart</code>). For skills
      alone, <code>/skills reload</code> also refreshes the available skills.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Details</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Author</strong> — <a href="https://github.com/jongio">Jon Gallant</a></li>
      <li><strong>Source</strong> — <a href="https://github.com/jongio/skills">github.com/jongio/skills</a></li>
      <li><strong>License</strong> — MIT</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .card pre {
    background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 9px;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; overflow-x: auto;
  }
</style>
